es in the windows height and width.",	// Disabled			"" ,	// Checked			"" 		// Other state		},		HMStringItem 		{			{ -1,0 }, { 0,0,0,0 },			"", "This view (FRAM) is used to frame the enclosed TStaticText.  It has a TSizeToParent sizer attached "			"which monitors its superview (MAIN) to adjusts its height and width according to changes in the "			"superview’s height and width.", "", "" 		},		HMStringItem 		{			{ -1,0 }, { 0,0,0,0 },			"", "This TStaticText view shows the example’s instructions.  It has a TSizeToParent sizer "			"which monitors its superview (FRAM) to adjusts its height and width according to changes in the "			"superview’s height and width.", "", "" 		}	}};resource 'hdlg' (1002) {	HelpMgrVersion, 0, hmDefaultOptions, 0, 5,	HMSkipItem {},	{		HMStringItem 		{			{ -1,0 }, { 0,0,0,0 },			"",		// Enabled			"This is the main view and it has a TSizeToParent sizer attached which monitors the window and "			"adjusts the view’s height and width according to changes in the windows height and width.",	// Disabled			"" ,	// Checked			"" 		// Other state		},		HMStringItem 		{			{ -1,0 }, { 0,0,0,0 },			"", "This view sticks to the right of the containing view using a TStickToRightOfParent behavior.", "", "" 		},		HMStringItem 		{			{ -1,0 }, { 0,0,0,0 },			"", "This view sticks to the bottom of the containing view using a TStickToBottomOfParent behavior.", "", "" 		},		HMStringItem 		{			{ -1,0 }, { 0,0,0,0 },			"", "This view sticks to the bottom right corner of the containing view using a TStickToBottomRightOfParent behavior.", "", "" 		}	}};resource 'hdlg' (1003) {	HelpMgrVersion, 0, hmDefaultOptions, 0, 5,	HMSkipItem {},	{		HMStringItem 		{			{ -1,0 }, { 0,0,0,0 }, 			"", "This example is very similar to “Show Sticky Views” with the exception that there is no main view.  "			"The three subviews are contained directly within the window.  This is meant to test that window "			"placement has no inadvertent effect on view resizing.", "" , ""		},		HMStringItem 		{			{ -1,0 }, { 0,0,0,0 },			"", "This view sticks to the right of the containing window using a TStickToRightOfParent behavior.", "", "" 		},		HMStringItem 		{			{ -1,0 }, { 0,0,0,0 },			"", "This view sticks to the bottom of the containing window using a TStickToBottomOfParent behavior.", "", "" 		},		HMStringItem 		{			{ -1,0 }, { 0,0,0,0 },			"", "This view sticks to the bottom right corner of the containing window using a TStickToBottomRightOfParent behavior.", "", "" 		}	}};resource 'hdlg' (1004) {	HelpMgrVersion, 0, hmDefaultOptions, 0, 5,	HMSkipItem {},	{		HMPictItem 		{			{ -1,0 }, { 0,0,10,10 },			1003,		// Enabled			1003,		// Disabled			1003,		// Checked			1003,		// Other state		},		HMPictItem 		{			{ -1,0 }, { 0,0,10,10 }, 			1002, 1002, 1002, 1002,		},		HMStringItem 		{			{ -1,0 }, { 0,0,0,0 },			"", "See the Red Rectangle, above, for an description of the views making up this "			"window, and see the Yellow Rectangle, also above, for a description of the sizers "			"used in this example.", "", "" 		},		HMStringItem 		{			{ -1,0 }, { 0,0,0,0 },			"", "This is the vertical divider view, 'DIVV' which is a sizer helper view.  Though it is visible in this "			"example, a sizer helper view does not necessarily need to be visible.  "			"The four colored rectangular views all have sizers which monitor this "			"view.", "", "" 		},		HMStringItem 		{			{ -1,0 }, { 0,0,0,0 },			"", "This is the horizontal divider view, 'DIVH' which is another sizer helper view.  "			"Its horizontal position is kept "			"proportional to the width of the main containing view.  "			"The four colored rectangular views all have sizers which monitor this "			"view.", "", "" 		}	}};